---
description: Shared local agent memory protocol (points to .agent/ and AGENTS.md)
alwaysApply: true
---

This repository uses a **shared local agent memory system**. This rule is a thin entry adapter — it
holds no project facts.

- Canonical protocol: `AGENTS.md` (see "§0. Local Agent Memory System").
- Canonical project memory: `.agent/`.

Before non-trivial changes, read hot context first:

1. `.agent/PROJECT_STATE.md`
2. `.agent/TASKS.md`
3. `.agent/HANDOFF.md`
4. `.agent/CONTEXT_INDEX.md`

Then read only the relevant `.agent/domains/*.md` (and deep `docs/*.md`) per `.agent/CONTEXT_INDEX.md`.
Do not load `.agent/logs/` or `.agent/archive/` unless explicitly tracing history.

Do not duplicate project state into Cursor rules. After meaningful progress, update the shared `.agent/`
memory files as defined in `AGENTS.md` §0.

Source-of-truth priority when things conflict: current code & tests → latest reproducible run →
`.agent/PROJECT_STATE.md` → `.agent/TASKS.md` → `.agent/domains/*.md` → `.agent/logs/` → `.agent/archive/`.
